  "id": "Compound::DB00451 - Gene::7067",
  "verbalization": "Levothyroxine is implicated in the pathogenesis of several disorders, including craniosynostosis, epiphysiolysis, and slipped femoral capital epiphysis, all of which are associated with Dextrothyroxine. These conditions are linked to the binding of Dextrothyroxine to Thra, a key component in the thyroid hormone signaling pathway. The shared mechanism of action between Levothyroxine and Dextrothyroxine, both of which are thyroid hormones, suggests a potential role in the regulation of Thra. The evidence from the visible paths indicates that Levothyroxine may influence Thra through a mechanism involving the thyroid hormone receptor, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The consistent association across multiple paths underscores the importance of thyroid hormone signaling in the pathophysiology of these conditions, and the observed binding of Dextrothyroxine to Thra provides a plausible biological basis for the observed effects.",
